<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Msauli yr shr slips into red, no div.</title>
<headline>Msauli yr shr slips into red, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - pre excepts	     16.1 loss   vs     80.8</p>
<p>- post excepts and</p>
<p>income appropriated for</p>
<p>exenditure on mining</p>
<p>    assets			53.7 loss   vs     16.7</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   nil	   vs     nil</p>
<p>    Attrib income		1.50 loss  vs	4.30</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			1.50 loss  vs	4.92</p>
<p>    Tax			   nil	   vs	0.62</p>
<p>    Interest received	  2.70	 vs	1.76</p>
<p>    Rationalisation costs    1.32	 vs	1.40</p>
<p>    Turnover		    75.12	 vs     94.11</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  0.58	 vs	1.40</p>
<p>Full name: Msauli Asbes Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said fibre production was down 37 percent for the year due to difficulties associated with deeper mining. Labour incidents and severe weather at the beginning of the year also contributed to the lower output.</p>
<p>Despite a 17 percent rise in income per ton due to the weakening rand, the profit margin was completely eroded by a 41 percent rise in the unit costs per ton, it said. As a result no dividend payment could be considered.</p>
<p>Prospects for any significant improvement from the current situation were remote, the group said, but it added that currency movements could have a significant impact on expected results.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
